 {
  "id": "F2",
  "title": "Marking the owner merged can resolve the landed round as superseded",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator lands a review round awaiting human attention whose original request closes the same issue as its parent. The factory permanently records that round as superseded instead of resolved by its merge.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/limitless-520-head-probe.ts\"",
    "output": "F2 after landed={\"status\":\"resolved\",\"merged\":true,\"resolution\":\"superseded\"}\nF2 after reconciliation={\"status\":\"resolved\",\"merged\":true,\"resolution\":\"superseded\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe created a succeeded owner and needs_human review round with the real Store, generated the round prompt with reviewRoundPrompt(), and invoked HEAD landed() with a MERGED observation. HEAD loops over '[run.id, owner.id]' and calls updateRun() with 'merged: true'. Store.updateRun() calls supersedeByIssue(), whose exclusion is only 'r.id !== merged.id'; consequently the owner update supersedes the still-needs_human round. Calling resolveMergedRun() afterward preserved that resolution. Base landed() updated only the entry's run: 'this.store.updateRun(run.id, { merged: true })', so this owner-triggered supersession was absent."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A review round that is waiting on a human gets approved and landed. Its prompt repeats the original request's 'Closes #N'. When the queue marks the parent run merged, the round that just landed is closed as 'superseded' by its own PR instead of 'merged'. Later reconciliation skips it, so the wrong resolution stays permanently.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "same scratch copy: a needs_human round and its owner both saying 'Closes #42'; land the round; print the resolutions. Run against head, and against a git-archive copy of base",
    "output": "HEAD: round: {\"merged\":true,\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolution\":{\"kind\":\"superseded\",\"ref\":\"https://github.com/test/repo/pull/1\",...}} owner: {\"merged\":true,\"status\":\"succeeded\"}\nBASE: round: {\"merged\":true,\"status\":\"needs_human\",\"resolution\":null} owner: {\"merged\":false,...} (reconciliation's resolveMergedRun later resolves it as merged)"
   },
   "evidence": "Head landed() loops over `new Set([run.id, owner.id])` and calls `this.store.updateRun(id, { merged: true, ... })`. updateRun runs `if (patch.merged) this.supersedeByIssue(run)`, which excludes only the run being updated. reviewRoundPrompt embeds `## Original request\\n${request}`, so the round's prompt keeps the 'Closes #N'. Base only updated the entry's run. At head, reconcileMergedRuns skips runs where `run.merged && run.status !== \"needs_human\"` and only fills metadata, so the superseded resolution is never corrected."
  }
 },
